          unit: '€',
          hint: 'Work out what one failure costs without the spare, then multiply by the yearly chance.',
          why: '800 × €500 = €400,000 per failure × 2% = €8,000 per year, about the same as a 20% holding cost (€8,000), so other factors decide.',
